00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.730
Let's all go in.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.070
No, Jack, you can't do that.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:48.210
Mary and Bob first.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:55.060
First mess I ever got in.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.720
Yeah, I told him five times.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:17:59.800
I said, Don.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:01.950
Haul up your wife.

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:03.950
Haul up the new wife.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:07.780
He ought to be a wise guy.

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:12.920
It's going to rain.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.640
If I get pneumonia, it'll be Don's fault.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:23.080
Rubbing your legs together.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.760
That's not me. That's a cricket.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:25.900
He's singing O Solo Mio.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.600
O Solo Mio?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.880
Sound like that to me.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.890
Well, that's because you don't understand Italian.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:39.360
You always have to annoy me.

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.060
Dennis, come on in.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:49.240
Yeah, I told my wife I saw Dennis ride up on his bicycle.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:54.000
Well, as long as you're dreaming things up, you're going to see me on the handlebars.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:55.240
Use your...

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:59.980
I was the two...

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:03.550
the fish holding up? Oh, there'll be plenty. Don't worry, Jack, you're next.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.480
Hey, look who's here, dear Dennis Day.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:19.210
I ought to have my head examined. Can't get over it. I told him once, I told him five times.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:20.810
It's just cold.

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:51.210
I knew we were going inside the house.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:51.930
Ready or not?

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.260
Stick them up, buddy.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:19:59.980
Please stick them up.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.170
Are you a burglar?

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.650
Who else works in lousy weather like this?

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.740
Mr. Keep those hands up.

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.090
Now, come on.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:14.910
Your money or your life?

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:24.130
They said your money or your life.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.010
I'm thinking it over.

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:37.480
Peep out of yule and say, help me, it's Christmas.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:38.440
But you heard him.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:39.500
He was calling me.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.990
The toilet face will be all gone.

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:51.960
Pretty out there, darling.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:53.900
Must have been mistaken.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:55.800
I guess I was there.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:05.800
You can't do this.

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:11.550
If Don Wilson had just taken my advice.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.730
What are you talking about?

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:15.710
I'll tell you what I'm talking about.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.000
If I told him what.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:19.800
I told him a thousand.

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:22.080
Don, I said.

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:24.810
Don, call up the little woman.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.260
White, smart.

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:44.440
And let's not barge in on the little...

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:47.340
I see.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:51.240
Then because of Mr. Wilson, you have this miserable cold.

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:54.430
A nervous shock from being held up.

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:59.370
Certainly understand your attitude, Mr. Benny.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.580
Oh, here's a copy of Mr. Wilson's contract.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:03.990
Look it over.

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:08.350
Well, you can see for yourself that this case should ever come to court.

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:11.900
Why, Mr. Wilson wouldn't have a leg to stand on.

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:14.340
Why, as a matter of fact, we might even...

00:22:14.340 --> 00:22:14.820
Wait a minute.

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:16.300
Wait a minute, Mr. Kearns.

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:16.460
Yeah?

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:17.640
Wait a minute.

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:21.030
I just noticed something.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.580
I don't want to fire down Wilson.

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:26.740
Jack, what made you change your mind?

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:29.740
You said yourself that he was responsible for your being sick.

00:22:30.670 --> 00:22:36.260
I know, but now that I see what I'm paying him, I deserve him.

00:22:43.990 --> 00:22:52.870
I know I'm getting bronchitis.

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:55.210
Well, it's your own fault for being so cheap.

00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:58.670
Anybody that has a cold as bad as you have would certainly call a doctor.

00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:01.620
I guess you're right, Mary.

00:23:02.470 --> 00:23:04.270
Who's a good doctor for bronchitis?

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:06.800
Well, I have a very good doctor.

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:07.920
His name's Dr. Hillary.

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:10.000
I'll call him.

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:12.700
What's his number?

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:17.370
Crestview-4199.

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:22.330
Crestview-544...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:38.260
So, Dr. Hillary, this is Take It or Lose It. For $5,000, what's the best way to treat bronchitis?

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:54.430
What? Not the right answer.

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:58.400
Well, I won't know for about three days.

00:24:05.244 --> 00:24:05.664
Good night.

00:24:15.612 --> 00:24:16.612
Thank you.
